Two new polymers, namely, PDTPO-IDT and PDTPO-IDTT, are synthesized by copolymerization of 4-(2-octyldodecyl)- dithieno[3,2-b:2’,3’-d]pyridin-5(4H)-one (DTPO) with indacenodithiophene (IDT) or indacenodithieno[3,2-b]thiophene (IDTT). The rational combination of well-planarity DTPO unit with the ladder-type IDT and IDTT units endows the resulting copolymers with wide optical bandgaps of ca. 2.05 eV, deep HOMO energy levels of ca. -5.32 eV and good holetransportingabilities with the hole mobility of $1.0\times10^{3}\mathsf{c m}^{2}\mathsf{V}^{1}\mathsf{s}^{1}$ .  The polymer solar cell (PSC) in a conventional structure based on PDTPO-IDT as donor and [6,6]-phenyl- ${\boldsymbol{\cdot}}{\mathsf{C}}_{71}$ -butyric acid methyl ester $({\mathsf{P C}}_{71}{\mathsf{B M}})$ as acceptor achieves a high power conversion efficiency (PCE) up to $7.33\%$ , the highest value for PSC based on polymers with optical bandgap over $2.0\mathsf{e V}$ to date, along with a remarkable open-circuit voltage $(V_{\mathrm{{oc}}})$ approaching $\begin{array}{r}{0.97\mathrm{V}.}\end{array}$ . The performance of PDTPO-IDTT based PSC is slightly behind with a moderate PCE of $5.47\%$ under the same condition. The relationship between the copolymer structures and optoelectronic properties as well as photovoltaics performances are comprehensively investigated in experiments and theoretical simulation.
## Introduction
Organic photovoltaics (OPVs), emerging as an environment benign technology with function of converting solar energy into electri city, have s hown a ttractive prospects owi ng to thei r low- cos t, li ghtwei ght, la rge-a rea and flexi ble fa bri cati on.1-8 Gratif yi ngl y, through i n-depth res earches on theori es9-11 a nd novel ma terials,5,12-16 the power conversi on efficienc y (PCE) of bulk heterojunction (BHJ) solar cells based on conjugated polymers as donors and [6,6]-phenyl- $\mathsf C_{71}/\mathsf C_{61}$ -butyric acid methyl ester ( $\mathsf{P C}_{71}\mathsf{B M}$ or $\mathsf{P C}_{61}\mathsf{B M}$ ) as acceptors have reached over $10\%$ f or si ngl e juncti on17-22 a nd $11\%$ f or ta ndem s ola r cells23,24. Such hi gh effi ciency pol ymer s olar cells (PSCs ) us uall y employed photoactive materials with low or medium bandgaps, for the purpose of enlarging incident light harvesting and originally promoting s hort circuit current density $(J_{s\mathsf{c}})$ . Compared to low and medium bandgap materials, wide bandgap materials have lagged behind, and only a few of them have achieved efficiencies over $7\%,^{25,26}$ i n particula r when the bandgap exceeds $2.0\ \mathsf{e V}$ . This is beca use s uch ki nds
of polymers suff er from an inherent def ection of narrow absorption band below $650\ \mathsf{n m}$ (optical bandgap $[E_{\mathrm{g}}]>1.9\mathsf{e V}$ ) in s olar s pectra, whi ch is not conduci ve to f ull y use hi gh lumi nous flux s ection of s ola r s pectra a nd directl y li mits the photocurrent at the firs t step of exciton generation. However, $J_{\mathrm{sc}}$ is only one of the key factors determining the efficiency of BHJ s ola r cells. T ha t mea ns we are a ble to opti mize the other two key factors: open circuit voltage $(V_{\circ\mathsf{c}})$ and fill fact or (FF) through reasonable material design and careful device process. Moreover, from a material engineering perspective, $J_{\mathsf{s c}}$ can be fine-tuned by effective exciton separation and enhance ment of charge-carrier mobility through the method of morphological control, device structure optimization as well as interlayer engineering. In addition, wide bandgap materials are critical to construct hi gh performa nce tandem s olar cells i n which they can be acted as photoactive layer in front cell of tandem solar cell combined with a rear cell using low bandgap materials to implement a full absorption of solar spectra.27,28
Ladder- type electron- donor units with linearly fused aromatic or heteroaromatic subunits have been widely utilized to buil d l ow a nd medium ba ndga p ma terials.29-32 This is because covalently forced planarization can extend effective conjugation length along polymer backbone and promote π- electron delocalization between parallel $p$ - orbitals. Moreover, structure i n ri gidifi ed copla nari ty ma y restrai n rotati onal disorder to lower reorganization energy, which benefits the charge carrier mobility. Indacenodithiophene (IDT) and indacenodithieno[3,2-b]thiophene (IDTT) are popular laddertype building blocks with five-membered and sevenmembered multifused rings, respectively. When they are copolymerized with common electron-deficient units, s uch as 4,7- di bromo- 2,1,3-benz othia diaz ole (BT ),31,33-35 4,7-dibromo5,6- difl uoro- 2,1,3- benz othi adi azol e (2FBT),34-36 1,3-dibromothi eno[ 3,4-c] pyrrol- 4,6- dione (TPD),35,37-39 the absorption spectra of the res ulting pol ymers of ten exhi bit a certai n extent blue shif ts compared with the polymers based on 4,8- bis(2- ethylhexyloxy)benzo[1,2-b:4,5-b’]dithiophene (BDTO) and 4,8- bis(5-(2-ethylhexyl)thiophen-2-yl)benzo[1,2-b:4,5-
b’] dithiophene (BDTT) coupled with similar acceptor unit. This means that both IDT and IDTT are weaker electron donors than benzodithiophenes (BDTs: BDTO and BDTT), which will facilitate wide bandgap.
Recently, Yu group and our group reported a novel structure of two thiophenes flanked tricyclic pyridone, namely, 4- (2- octyldodecyl)-dithieno[3,2- b:2’,3’- d]pyridin- $5(4H)-$ one (DTPO).40,41 The copolymers based on DTPO and BDTs (PDTPOBDTO and PDTPO-BDTT) showed bandgaps around 2.0 eV and a relatively deep HOMO energy level of $-5.44\mathrm{~eV}$ which led to a high $V_{\mathsf{o c}}$ of $0.98{\sf V}.$ , and PCEs up to $6.84\%$ were achieved in PSCs Meanwhile, the homopolymer of DTPO revealed a high hole mobility i n organi c filed-eff ect transis tor (OFET). Thes e resul ts indicated that DTPO is a good building block for wide bandgap materials.
Aiming to explore new wide bandgap materials, herein, we designed and synthesized two new polymers, namely, PDTPOIDT and PDTPO-IDTT (Scheme 1), by replacing BDTs with IDT and IDTT units as electron donors to copolymerize with DTPO unit. We anticipate that the combination of the ladder-type IDT and IDTT units with DTPO unit would facilitate the planarization of the copolymers, strengthen intermol ecular π- π stacking and improve the charge- carrier transporting properties. The two copolymers show wide bandgaps of ca. $2.05\ \mathsf{e V}$ . Noticeably, PSCs based on PDTPO-IDT exhibited high $V_{\infty}$ up to $0.98\mathrm{~V~}$ and achieved PCEs up to $7.33\%$ .
