## Fabrication and characterization of solar cells
Polymer solar cells (PSCs ) with a conventional device structure of $170/\mathsf{P E D O T:P S S/p o l\upgamma m e r:P C_{71}B M/C a/A l}$ were fabricated. The patterned ITO-coated glass was scrubbed by detergent and then cleaned inside an ultrasonic bath by using deionized water, acetone, and isopropyl alcohol sequentially, and dried overnight in an oven before use. Then, PEDOT:PSS (Heraeus Clevios P VP A 4083) layer was spin-coated onto the ITO with a thi ckness of $40\ n m$ , and then dried at $150^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ under air condition f or 10 min. Next, the photoactive layer with a opti mal thi ckness of $85\ \mathsf{n m}$ was prepared by spin casting the mixed solution of PDTPO-IDT (or PDTPO-IDTT) and $\mathsf{P C}_{71}\mathsf{B M}$ i n $o$ -dichlorobenzene (the concentration of PDTPO-IDT or PDTPO-IDTT is $10\:\mathrm{\mg/ml}$ f or all bl e nd fil ms ) wi th diff erent weight ratio and DIO concentration at 1600 rpm for 40 s on the top of PEDOT:PSS layer. After that, methanol was spi ncoated atop the PDTPO-IDT (or PDTPO-IDTT): $\mathsf{P C}_{71}\mathsf{B M}$ blend layer at 2500 rpm for $30~\mathfrak{s}$ before the deposition of cathode. Fi nall y, a $20\ \mathsf{n m}$ Ca and 100 nm Al layer were subsequently evaporated onto the active layer through a shadow mask at a vacuum pressure of $\approx5\times{10}^{-5}$ Pa to form top electrode. The overlapping proportion between cathode and anode is 4.5 $\mathsf{m}\mathsf{m}^{2}$ . In order to accurately meas ure the perf ormance of PSCs, an aperture with the area of $3.14~\mathsf{m m}^{2}$ was used. The currentvoltage $\left(J-V\right)$ characteristics were conduc ted by using a Keithley 2400 Source Measure Unit. Solar cell performance wa s carried out under i rra dia tion i ntensi ty of $100~\mathsf{m w~c m}^{-2}$ meas ured by a calibrated silicon s olar cell and a readout meter (Model 91150V, Newport) from an Air Mass 1.5 Global (AM 1.5 G) sol ar si mulator (Class AAA s olar si mula tor, Model 94063A, Oriel). The EQE spectra were measured using a QEX10 Solar Cell IPCE measurement system (PV measurement, Inc). All the fabrication process es were carried out inside a dry glovebox filled with nitrogen expect for the spin-coating of PEDOT:PSS.
